{
  "_id": "ecclesiastes1",
  "book": {
    "_id": "ecclesiastes",
    "title": "Ecclesiastes",
    "titleShort": "Eccl.",
    "titleOfficial": "OR, THE PREACHER",
    "subtitle": "",
    "summary": "",
    "chapterDelineation": "Chapter"
  },
  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Ecclesiastes",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "Everything under the sun is vanity and vexation of spirit—He who increases in knowledge increases in sorrow.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "The words of the Preacher, the son of David, king in Jerusalem.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "Eccl. 7:27."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Vanity of vanities, saith the Preacher, vanity of vanities; all is vanity.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 6,
            "text": "TG Vanity."
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "IE empty, fleeting, unsubstantial."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 66
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "What profit hath a man of all his labour which he taketh under the sun?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 11,
            "text": "1 Sam. 12:21; Matt. 16:26; 2 Ne. 9:51."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "One generation passeth away, and another generation cometh: but the earth abideth for ever.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "TG Earth, Destiny of."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 40
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The sun also ariseth, and the sun goeth down, and hasteth to his place where he arose.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The wind goeth toward the south, and turneth about unto the north; it whirleth about continually, and the wind returneth again according to his circuits.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 140,
            "end": 152,
            "text": "OR its circuit."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "All the rivers run into the sea; yet the sea is not full; unto the place from whence the rivers come, thither they return again.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 47
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "All things are full of labour; man cannot utter it: the eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor the ear filled with hearing.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 76,
            "text": "Prov. 27:20."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The thing that hath been, it is that which shall be; and that which is done is that which shall be done: and there is no new thing under the sun.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 121,
            "end": 124,
            "text": "Eccl. 3:15."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 29,
            "end": 36
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 78
          },
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 117
          },
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 130
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Is there any thing whereof it may be said, See, this is new? it hath been already of old time, which was before us.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 12
          },
          {
            "start": 53,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There is no remembrance of former things; neither shall there be any remembrance of things that are to come with those that shall come after.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 23,
            "text": "TG Veil."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 41
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 68
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 90
          },
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 118
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I the Preacher was king over Israel in Jerusalem.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And I gave my heart to seek and search out by wisdom concerning all things that are done under heaven: this sore travail hath God given to the sons of man to be exercised therewith.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 52,
            "text": "D&C 97:1 (1–2)."
          },
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 120,
            "text": "HEB (literally) “evil business”; i.e., that which is of little profit. Eccl. 4:8."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 68,
            "end": 74
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I have seen all the works that are done under the sun; and, behold, all is vanity and vexation of spirit.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 75,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "TG Vanity."
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "HEB striving after wind; thus, frustration. Eccl. 2:17 (17, 26); 4:4 (4, 6, 16); 6:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 74
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "That which is crooked cannot be made straight: and that which is wanting cannot be numbered.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 21,
            "text": "Eccl. 7:13."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 13
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I communed with mine own heart, saying, Lo, I am come to great estate, and have gotten more wisdom than all they that have been before me in Jerusalem: yea, my heart had great experience of wisdom and knowledge.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "HEB I have become great."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 112
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "And I gave my heart to know wisdom, and to know madness and folly: I perceived that this also is vexation of spirit.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "Eccl. 7:25; Mosiah 12:27."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For in much wisdom is much grief: and he that increaseth knowledge increaseth sorrow.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 66,
            "text": "TG Knowledge."
          },
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 84,
            "text": "TG Sorrow."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 19,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "nextChapterId": "ecclesiastes2",
  "prevChapterId": "proverbs31",
  "volume": {
    "_id": "oldtestament",
